;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 by the user (written by Claude, from design
;; section 16 and the guest runs). Why this is right:
;; - VMS's own message for the fault, SS$_FLTOVF_F, at SHORT(1.0D300),
;;   then its traceback: the module's initializer, called from the
;;   program's start. tools/vax-suite masks the code addresses, which
;;   any change to the code moves.
;; - Only here, not in standard output too: the program had written to
;;   SYS$OUTPUT before the fault (a guest test, 2026-10-10, showed VMS's
;;   message only in a SYS$OUTPUT file the program had not opened).
;; - For every build but -OC -range-checks, whose own expected-vax-
;;   rangechecks-OC-range-checks-1.err overrides it.
%SYSTEM-F-FLTOVF_F, arithmetic fault, floating overflow at PC=xxxxxxxx, PSL=xxxxxxxx
%TRACE-F-TRACEBACK, symbolic stack dump follows
module name     routine name                     line       rel PC    abs PC

RANGECHECKS     RANGECHECKS_INIT                           xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
RANGECHECKS     RANGECHECKS_MAIN                           xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
